<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Palaces of Abomey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Palaces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abomey">Abomey</a> are the complex of earthen palaces built by the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> at Abomey, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, from the 17th to the 19th century. Successive kings added their own palaces, decorated with painted bas-reliefs recording the kingdom's history and beliefs. The site was inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 1985 and houses a historical museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-palaces-of-abomey.jpg" alt="Royal Palaces of Abomey" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joachim Huber · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abomey_2006_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
